From eb1afafd742532e08edd0bf62660d8f01428af3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:32:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0031-vela-dx11-probe: VELA_DX11_PROBE=1 reads what crosses
 the DX11 -> DX12 bridge once per feature at its 120th Evaluate (again 120
 frames after each Vela live model switch): a = the game's D3D11 inputs, a2 =
 the shared colour through D3D11, b = the shared inputs through a D3D12
 readback, c = the shared output through D3D12, c2 = the shared output through
 D3D11, d = the game's output after the copy back (per channel
 min/max/mean/naninf, a texel-byte hash, the centre pixel), plus preExposure /
 exposure and each shared texture's D3D11 and D3D12 desc, Vulkan format and
 layouts (Ghostrunner DX11: scene white / black on FSR 4 and SGSR 2);
 VELA_DX11_SHARED_BIND=1 (opt-in A/B, not a fix) makes the bridge's own shared
 copies with the fewest bind flags

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
